From b811ed8e039fe8fd6647e081448b2060e9618dcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:43:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compartments: add the policy service of Compartments
 (ADR-208)

One store of profiles per package in system_server, written only by the exit app
(MANAGE_COMPARTMENTS) and readable for one label by Settings
(READ_COMPARTMENT_PROFILE). The pure core (Profiles, PolicyStore, MirrorPlan) is
host-tested in privacy/compartments-profiles. The service mirrors the store to
the settings hardening list (ADR-175), the USE_LOOPBACK_INTERFACE permission and
the file that the sensor service reads (ADR-167); each mirror stands alone. A
store that cannot be read reads as Protected for every app. The event log
records the class and value, never the package.
